From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M3 Pro Linux downstream <m3pro-linux@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:01:00 -0500
Subject: [DEVELOPMENT PATCH 2/3] arm64: dts: apple: t6030: include GPU
 candidate for J514s and J516s

Development only. Include t6030-gpu.dtsi from t6030.dtsi, after
t6030-pmgr.dtsi defines ps_gfx. The GPU is SoC-level hardware, so both
M3 Pro boards get the same disabled nodes through their existing
t6030.dtsi include: t6030-j514s.dts (14-inch) and t6030-j516s.dts
(16-inch). Neither board file changes.

Each board DTB gains only the disabled gpu@0 and mbox@0 nodes, the
gpu_opp sentinel table and six disabled reserved-memory children. No
existing node or property changes, and no new DTC warning appears at
the default or W=1 level.

The node still carries only the generic "apple,agx-g15s" compatible.
The gpu alias that a loader uses to fill the node is deliberately not
added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
index efa9e57..529bf0f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6030.dtsi
@@ -1534,3 +1534,4 @@
 };
 
 #include "t6030-pmgr.dtsi"
+#include "t6030-gpu.dtsi"
